    "result_text": "There's only one test class, and the full suite is green.\n\nDone. The change adds `telephoneDisplay` while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\n**What I did (three files, minimal structural impact):**\n\n1. **New tiny helper** `TelephoneDisplay.java` \u2014 a single-purpose static formatter with no surrounding class complexity. It splits the country code (1 digit for `+1`/`+7`, else 2 \u2014 matching this Australia-defaulting app) from the national number and groups the national digits in threes: `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line on `toOwnerDto` delegating to the helper. No existing method grew; `owner.getTelephone()` is already the stored E.164 value at mapping time.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared `telephoneDisplay` as a `readOnly` derived property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field. `telephone` remains the raw E.164 field, untouched.\n\nThe new acceptance test (`telephone` = `+61412345678`, `telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`) and the full suite pass.",
